{
  "summary": "You established a strong, well-justified mission rationale in the 'Mission Concept & Rationale' section addressing Australian reef monitoring. To progress to higher rubric bands, you need to rectify a major orbital mechanics error, incorporate contingency planning and explicit information sources into your project plan, present actual preliminary mission engineering calculations or simulation outputs, and standardise your referencing and figure captions.",
  "next_steps": [
    "Correct your orbital design in 'Project Plan & Preliminary Progress': recalculate parameters recognising that geostationary orbit is ~35,786 km at the equator, whereas a 600 km altitude represents Low Earth Orbit.",
    "Produce tangible preliminary engineering results (such as initial orbital propagation, coverage analyses, or payload hand calculations) rather than citing tutorial completions.",
    "Upgrade report formatting by replacing raw URL footnotes with complete bibliographic citations, adding formal captions to figures, and incorporating schedule contingencies and future information sources into your plan."
  ],
  "criteria": {
    "C1": "You clearly defined mission goals and demonstrated strong relevance to Australian conservation users. To reach the top of Accomplished, provide more detailed quantitative mission requirements and explicit technical specifications alongside your functional narrative.",
    "C2": "Your Gantt chart effectively outlines tasks, achieving Adequate. To reach Accomplished, correct the orbital mechanics logic (a 600 km orbit cannot be geostationary), identify planned literature and data sources, and incorporate explicit project variations and contingency management.",
    "C3": "Listing completed STK tutorials shows preliminary effort but does not supply mission-specific results. To reach Adequate or Accomplished, calculate and display actual technical progress, such as baseline orbital trades, access times, or preliminary sizing data.",
    "C4": "Your document uses a readable, logical structure. To reach Accomplished, ensure all figures include formal descriptive captions and replace raw URL footnotes with fully detailed, consistently formatted academic references."
  }
}
